# Read-Only Root Filesystem with Boot-Time Config Generation

## Goal
Run a Raspberry Pi node with a read-only (RO) root filesystem while still allowing user settings changes by regenerating required files at boot into a writable runtime location.

## Core Idea
- Keep `/` mounted RO to prevent SD corruption from runtime writes.
- Store user-editable config on writable storage (separate partition/drive) e.g. `/data/`.
- At boot, generate all derived configs and unit files into `/run` (tmpfs, writable).
- Point services at generated files via symlinks (or direct paths).

## Filesystem Roles
- `/` : RO root filesystem (static base image)
- `/run` : RW tmpfs (RAM-backed, exists early in boot)
- `/data` : RW persistent storage for user config (separate partition/SSD/etc)

## Boot Sequence
1. System boots; `/run` is available (tmpfs).
2. `nucleus-gen.service` runs early.
3. Generator reads `/data/nucleus/config.*`.
4. Generator writes outputs into `/run/nucleus/...`.
5. Generator creates/updates symlinks from expected locations to `/run/nucleus/...`.
6. systemd starts the rest of the stack using those symlinked/generated files.

## Example Paths
Persistent user config:
- `/data/nucleus/config.yaml`

Generated at boot (runtime only):
- `/run/nucleus/wpa_supplicant.conf`
- `/run/nucleus/hostapd.conf`
- `/run/nucleus/babeld.conf`
- `/run/nucleus/smcroute.conf`
- `/run/nucleus/mesh.service` (if you generate units)

Symlinks (examples):
- `/etc/nucleus/hostapd.conf -> /run/nucleus/hostapd.conf`
- `/etc/nucleus/babeld.conf -> /run/nucleus/babeld.conf`
- `/etc/systemd/system/mesh.service -> /run/nucleus/mesh.service`

## systemd Unit (oneshot generator)
Create:
- `/etc/systemd/system/nucleus-gen.service`

Contents:
- Ensure it runs before network/services that depend on generated files.

Example:
[Unit]
Description=Generate Nucleus runtime config
DefaultDependencies=no
Before=network-pre.target

[Service]
Type=oneshot
ExecStart=/usr/local/bin/nucleus-gen.sh

[Install]
WantedBy=multi-user.target

Enable:
- `systemctl enable nucleus-gen.service`

## Generator Responsibilities (nucleus-gen.sh)
Must:
- Create `/run/nucleus`
- Read persistent config from `/data/nucleus/config.yaml`
- Generate all derived configs into `/run/nucleus/`
- Create symlinks into expected paths (where consumers look)
- Optionally call `systemctl daemon-reload` if generating unit files

## Minimal Command Pattern (concept)
- Make runtime dir writable:
  - `mkdir -p /run/nucleus`
- Generate files into `/run/nucleus/...`
- Symlink expected paths -> `/run/nucleus/...`
- Keep `/` mounted RO (or remount RO after generation if needed):
  - `mount -o remount,ro /`

## Constraints
- Anything that must persist across reboots cannot live only in `/run` (tmpfs).
- Keep persistent user config on a writable volume (e.g. `/data`).
- Services must start after generation (use `Before=` and dependencies as needed).
